{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYBjodjUWLaDKQCrKVij","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wk24HoEUzMdTpg77fhHvdE","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md","old_string":"- Formal: see bottom of this file.","new_string":"- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  checks_si.cfg / ALTOPS): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt,\n  including insn_div/divu/rem/remu, reg, liveness, unique, causal, ill.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (Gowin, place_option 0): **44.7 MHz** (was\n  5.44), 23 logic levels; logic 2435 LUTs (was ~12.3k), 668 regs, 6 DSP.\n  Worst paths are now regfile/ID/EX -> forward -> ALU -> dmem address."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":117968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef1999f9-5500-4d58-b463-00f007f7fcc8","uuid":"dc06b8fc-aa9e-4660-bb5f-8c23740ac782","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:14:44.254Z","request_id":"req_011CfYBjnndyzEggo4hK2f4D"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Wk24HoEUzMdTpg77fhHvdE", "type": "tool_result", "content": "The file /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ef1999f9-5500-4d58-b463-00f007f7fcc8", "uuid": "91772a10-bb91-465e-a372-bafea4ed4149", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:14:44.267Z", "tool_use_result": {"filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "oldString": "- Formal: see bottom of this file.", "newString": "- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  checks_si.cfg / ALTOPS): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt,\n  including insn_div/divu/rem/remu, reg, liveness, unique, causal, ill.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (Gowin, place_option 0): **44.7 MHz** (was\n  5.44), 23 logic levels; logic 2435 LUTs (was ~12.3k), 668 regs, 6 DSP.\n  Worst paths are now regfile/ID/EX -> forward -> ALU -> dmem address.", "originalFile": "# Implementation notes — sequential radix-2 divider\n\n## What changed\n\n- `rtl/divider.sv` (new): FSM `IDLE -> ABS -> RUN x32 -> FIX -> DONE`.\n  - IDLE + `req`: latch raw post-forward operands `a_q`/`b_q`, `is_signed`\n    (`!funct3[0]`), `want_rem` (`funct3[1]`).\n  - ABS: `quo <= |a|`, `dvs <= |b|` (magnitude only for signed ops),\n    `rem <= 0`, precompute `neg_q = signed && (a31^b31) && b!=0` and\n    `neg_r = signed && a31`. Doing abs a cycle after the latch keeps the\n    forward-mux -> negate path out of the start cycle.\n  - RUN: one 34-bit trial subtract `{0,rem,quo[31]} - {00,dvs}` + shift per\n    cycle, 5-bit counter, 32 iterations.\n  - FIX: `result_q <= neg ? -sel : sel` (sel = rem or quo); registered, so\n    EX only adds one mux arm to the `alu_result` capture.\n  - DONE: holds `done` until `ack` (= EX/MEM captured).\n  - Div-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 fall out of the loop (q=all-ones, r=a;\n    q=0x80000000, r=0) with no special compare.\n  - `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`: `IDLE -> FIX -> DONE`, result is the\n    riscv-formal `(a_q - b_q) ^ const` from the latched operands. The\n    start/stall/latch/ack handshake is still exercised in BMC.\n  - Latency: div sits in ID/EX 36 cycles (3 under ALTOPS).\n- `core_pkg.sv` / `decoder.sv` / `id_stage.sv`: new `ctrl_t.is_div` bit, set\n  for funct7=0x01 with funct3[2]=1 inside the already-validated R-type arm\n  (illegal-default discipline unchanged). A flop bit keeps `div_busy` one\n  LUT deep (`valid & is_div & !done`), since it fans out to PC/ID-EX enables.\n- `ex_stage.sv`: instantiates the divider (req = `in.valid && is_div`,\n  ack = `done && !stall`). New `div_busy` output. While busy, EX/MEM\n  captures a bubble (`ctrl <= '0`, `valid <= 0`) unless the dmem-stall hold\n  applies (hold has priority). On done, `alu_result` takes `div_result` and\n  `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` take the latched `a_q`/`b_q` for exact RVFI rs?_rdata.\n- `hazard_unit.sv`: `div_busy` input asserts `stall_if` and `stall_id`\n  (hold, no flush). flush_id can't fire while a div is in ID/EX\n  (load_use needs a load in ID/EX, redirect needs a branch/jump there).\n- `core.sv`: wires `div_busy` from ex_stage to hazard_unit. Top-level IO\n  unchanged.\n- `alu.sv`: removed the `/` and `%` arms (real and ALTOPS). Div op codes\n  fall to `default: out = 0`. MUL* and ALTOPS MUL* unchanged.\n- Tests: `test_alu.py` drops the divide vectors (checks div ops return 0);\n  new `test_divider.py` ports all DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors (div-by-zero,\n  INT_MIN/-1, sign mixes, back-to-back, 200 random vs a Python RV32M\n  reference) and checks operand latching (inputs scrambled after the start\n  edge) plus a_q/b_q. `test_pipeline.py` source list gained `divider.sv`.\n\n## Deviations from the plan\n\n- No separate `bubble_ex` hazard output: ex_stage computes the bubble\n  itself from `div_busy` with the existing `stall` (dmem hold) taking\n  priority, which is the same logic.\n- Added a separate ABS cycle (plan did abs at start) for a shorter start\n  path; costs one extra cycle per divide.\n\n## Verification status\n\n- Verilator lint `-Wall`: clean, with and without `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- cocotb: alu 14, decoder 30, divider 8, pipeline 11 — all pass.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` (needs `NRET=1` in env locally): passed,\n  selftest + CoreMark (selftest has 4 divides, CoreMark 5 static).\n- Formal: see bottom of this file.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- Divide-heavy code loses ~35 cycles per divide; CoreMark's timed window\n  has almost none.\n- Divider data regs (`a_q`, `rem`, `quo`, ...) have no reset; they are\n  always written before being read (state/done are reset).\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 56, "oldLines": 7, "newStart": 56, "newLines": 12, "lines": [" - cocotb: alu 14, decoder 30, divider 8, pipeline 11 — all pass.", " - `make cosim TARGET=bench` (needs `NRET=1` in env locally): passed,", "   selftest + CoreMark (selftest has 4 divides, CoreMark 5 static).", "-- Formal: see bottom of this file.", "+- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,", "+  checks_si.cfg / ALTOPS): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt,", "+  including insn_div/divu/rem/remu, reg, liveness, unique, causal, ill.", "+- `make timing TARGET=bench` (Gowin, place_option 0): **44.7 MHz** (was", "+  5.44), 23 logic levels; logic 2435 LUTs (was ~12.3k), 668 regs, 6 DSP.", "+  Worst paths are now regfile/ID/EX -> forward -> ALU -> dmem address.", " ", " ## Concerns", " "]}], "userModified": false, "replaceAll": false}}
