{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYBjLzcKUdZWUSPHemqB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E67BcNT3Uk2hU9V7PHqQiL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md","old_string":"- Formal: see below.","new_string":"- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  auto-detected nret=1): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (place option 0): **Fmax 46.50 MHz** (was 5.44),\n  19 logic levels. Logic 2399 LUTs (was 12312), 673 regs, 2 DSPs.\n  - Top paths (~26.7 ns): regfile -> ID -> EX -> IF redirect -> hazard ->\n    ID/EX (redirect/flush), and regfile -> EX -> ALU add -> dmem BSRAM\n    address.\n  - No MDU logic is on the top paths, as the hypothesis predicted. The next\n    Fmax lever is the redirect path, not the M-unit."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":119445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":793},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7ff24e0-f7ed-49cf-8633-27fbbaea47cb","uuid":"c7707ad0-b108-468c-aa3e-30819deebf3a","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:14:40.605Z","request_id":"req_011CfYBjLWqBTq9fb4RYFXB6"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01E67BcNT3Uk2hU9V7PHqQiL", "type": "tool_result", "content": "The file /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c7ff24e0-f7ed-49cf-8633-27fbbaea47cb", "uuid": "10dfdeb8-05eb-4381-96d4-ea33eb6f4835", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:14:40.623Z", "tool_use_result": {"filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "oldString": "- Formal: see below.", "newString": "- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  auto-detected nret=1): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (place option 0): **Fmax 46.50 MHz** (was 5.44),\n  19 logic levels. Logic 2399 LUTs (was 12312), 673 regs, 2 DSPs.\n  - Top paths (~26.7 ns): regfile -> ID -> EX -> IF redirect -> hazard ->\n    ID/EX (redirect/flush), and regfile -> EX -> ALU add -> dmem BSRAM\n    address.\n  - No MDU logic is on the top paths, as the hypothesis predicted. The next\n    Fmax lever is the redirect path, not the M-unit.", "originalFile": "# Implementation notes: multi-cycle stalling M-unit\n\n## What changed\n- `rtl/mdu.sv` (new): multi-cycle RV32M unit. `start`/`hold`/`done` handshake,\n  latched post-forward operands (`a_lat`/`b_lat`).\n  - MUL*: one shared 33x33 signed product. Operands are sign- or zero-extended\n    per op into input regs, then a product reg, then a low/high-half select\n    from the product reg. 2 stall cycles.\n  - DIV/REM*: radix-2 restoring divider on magnitudes. INIT (magnitudes),\n    32 iterations of one 33-bit subtract + shift, then FIN (sign fix-up into\n    a result reg). About 35 stall cycles. RV32M special cases come out of the\n    magnitude algorithm, so there is no separate early-out:\n    - divide by 0: q = all ones and r = dividend. The quotient sign fix is\n      suppressed when the divisor is 0.\n    - INT_MIN/-1: |q| = 2^31, and negating it gives INT_MIN; r = 0.\n  - `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`: same handshake, but it computes the ALTOPS\n    formulas at launch into a result reg (1 stall cycle). The real datapath\n    is `ifdef`'d out, so the solver never sees it.\n- `rtl/alu.sv`: now RV32I only. The M-ext arms (real and ALTOPS) and the\n  three 64-bit products are gone.\n- `rtl/core_pkg.sv` / `rtl/decoder.sv` / `rtl/id_stage.sv`: new\n  `ctrl.is_mdu` bit, set for legal OP with funct7=0000001. Legality logic is\n  unchanged.\n- `rtl/ex_stage.sv`:\n  - `mdu_stall = in.valid && in.ctrl.is_mdu && !mdu_done`. This uses\n    registered state only (ID/EX flops + the MDU done flop), as the\n    hypothesis required. It is also the MDU `start`; the MDU ignores it while\n    busy.\n  - Priority: `stall` (dmem) holds EX/MEM; otherwise `mdu_stall` puts a\n    bubble (`'0`) into EX/MEM.\n  - On completion EX/MEM takes `alu_result = mdu_result`, and takes\n    rs1_val/rs2_val/write_data from the MDU's latched operands.\n  - `hold` is wired to the dmem stall, so done/result persist until EX/MEM\n    actually captures them.\n- `rtl/hazard_unit.sv`: `mdu_stall` input ORed into `stall_if` and\n  `stall_id`. `flush_id` is unchanged: an M-op in ID/EX is never a load or a\n  branch/jump, so load-use and redirect can't fire at the same time.\n- `rtl/core.sv`: wires `mdu_stall`.\n- Tests:\n  - New `test/test_mdu.py` (clocked). It has all the former M-ext vectors\n    plus a few extra ones, and it scrambles the live operands after launch\n    to prove the unit uses its latched copies. It also covers hold/done\n    persistence and back-to-back launches.\n  - `test_alu.py` now has RV32I vectors only.\n  - `test_pipeline.py` adds mdu.sv to its sources, plus two tests: a\n    MUL->DIV->ADD->REMU dependent chain (checks RVFI rs1/rs2 and order), and\n    an M-op followed by load-use and a taken branch that uses the M-op\n    result.\n\n## Deviations\n- There is no explicit early-out for divide-by-0 or INT_MIN/-1. The\n  magnitude divider gives the RV32M results directly, so this is less logic;\n  it costs about 35 cycles on those rare ops.\n- The MUL result is selected from the product reg straight into EX/MEM (no\n  extra result reg), so MUL costs 2 stall cycles, not 3.\n- The M-ext test used by `test/test_pipeline.py` does not exercise a dmem\n  stall. The cocotb harness has no stall model; the dmem-stall interaction\n  is covered by cosim (random stalls on both buses) and by formal.\n\n## Concerns\n- Whether Gowin packs the 33x33 multiply's in/out regs into the DSP. If it\n  doesn't, a+b regs -> product reg is still a single multiply per cycle, off\n  the redirect path.\n\n## Local status\n- Verilator lint (-Wall): clean, both with and without ALTOPS.\n- cocotb: alu 9, decoder 30, mdu 15, pipeline 13 tests, 0 failures.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` (NRET=1): passed (selftest + CoreMark).\n- Formal: see below.\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 66, "oldLines": 4, "newStart": 66, "newLines": 12, "lines": [" - Verilator lint (-Wall): clean, both with and without ALTOPS.", " - cocotb: alu 9, decoder 30, mdu 15, pipeline 13 tests, 0 failures.", " - `make cosim TARGET=bench` (NRET=1): passed (selftest + CoreMark).", "-- Formal: see below.", "+- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,", "+  auto-detected nret=1): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the first attempt.", "+- `make timing TARGET=bench` (place option 0): **Fmax 46.50 MHz** (was 5.44),", "+  19 logic levels. Logic 2399 LUTs (was 12312), 673 regs, 2 DSPs.", "+  - Top paths (~26.7 ns): regfile -> ID -> EX -> IF redirect -> hazard ->", "+    ID/EX (redirect/flush), and regfile -> EX -> ALU add -> dmem BSRAM", "+    address.", "+  - No MDU logic is on the top paths, as the hypothesis predicted. The next", "+    Fmax lever is the redirect path, not the M-unit."]}], "userModified": false, "replaceAll": false}}
