{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bko8kbuye","tool_use_id":"toolu_011ir5HFZQoo7CfHgZpbjBBJ","status":"completed","output_file":"/srv/hwebench/tmp/69e3cb52/42c25cd1/claude-1003/-srv-hwebench-clones-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-v2-rep2-cores-bench-worktrees-hyp-20260929-002-r2s1/4ec48193-9760-431e-8182-33e571c58677/tasks/bko8kbuye.output","summary":"Background command \"Run Gowin timing analysis\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"49c6aa15-5174-4fea-a14f-89fdda67831a","session_id":"4ec48193-9760-431e-8182-33e571c58677"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfYDCaz71v3reiniKbEy7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RHVro4SBhEMkegQQgjnZ1d", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes: valid-bit squash pipeline control\n\n## What changed\n\n- **if_stage.sv**: the `(flush||redirect) ? NOP : imem_data` mux is gone.\n  `out.instr = imem_data`, `out.valid = imem_ready` (new `imem_ready`\n  input). The `flush` input is removed. PC priority is unchanged\n  (reset > redirect > !stall > hold).\n- **id_stage.sv**: ports are now `hold`/`squash` (they replace\n  `stall`/`flush`). Decoder, imm_gen, regfile addresses and the ID/EX\n  rd/rs fields all use the raw fetched word. The ID/EX data fields have\n  no reset and no flush and load whenever `!hold`. A separate `valid_q`\n  flop resets to 0 and otherwise loads `in.valid && !squash` when `!hold`.\n- **hazard_unit.sv**: `load_use = id_ex.valid && id_ex.mem_read &&\n  rd!=0 && (rd==imem_data[19:15] || rd==imem_data[24:20])` (raw word).\n  Outputs are `stall_if` (same terms as before),\n  `id_hold = dmem_stall || mdu_stall`,\n  `id_squash = load_use || redirect`, and `stall_ex_mem`/`hold_mem_wb`\n  (unchanged). `flush_if`/`flush_id` are removed.\n- **ex_stage.sv**:\n  - `redirect = in.valid && (taken || jump) && !misalign`.\n  - The EX/MEM register is split. `ctrl_q`/`valid_q` reset to 0 and hold\n    on stall. They capture `ex_valid = in.valid && !mdu_stall`, with\n    reg_write/mem_read/mem_write/is_illegal/is_mdu ANDed with `ex_valid`.\n    The data fields have no reset and hold only on dmem stall. The\n    mdu_stall bubble is therefore now \"valid=0 + side effects cleared\"\n    instead of a full `'0` reset.\n  - Step 6: there is a new dedicated `mem_addr = rs1_fwd + imm` adder,\n    captured into the new `ex_mem_t.mem_addr` field.\n- **mem_stage.sv**: dmem_addr, byte_mask, misalign, load shift and the\n  RVFI aligned_addr now come from `in.mem_addr` instead of\n  `in.alu_result`. `alu_result` still feeds forwarding and writeback.\n- **core_pkg.sv**: adds `mem_addr` to `ex_mem_t`. Comments updated.\n- **core.sv**: rewired. The hazard unit gets `id_ex.valid` and the raw\n  `io_imemData` rs fields. No IO or RVFI changes.\n- **forward_unit.sv**: unchanged. EX/MEM reg_write is valid-qualified\n  at capture.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- **Step 5 not done** (registered forward selects). It is optional in\n  the hypothesis and I left it out to keep the risk and the time budget\n  down.\n- **No extra valid gating on dmem_wen/dmem_ren in mem_stage.** EX/MEM\n  mem_read/mem_write are already cleared for every invalid slot, and\n  ctrl_q resets to 0, so the extra AND would only add logic.\n- The ID/EX and EX/MEM `reg_q.valid` / `reg_q.ctrl` sub-fields are still\n  written (to a constant or unused value) so Verilator sees them driven.\n  `out.valid`/`out.ctrl` are overridden from the separate flops, and\n  synthesis prunes the unused bits.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint (`-Wall`): clean.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  auto nret=1 → wrapper_si + checks_si): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the\n  first attempt. Note: passing `formal/checks.cfg` explicitly forces the\n  nret=2 wrapper and fails at elaboration with \"no io_rvfi_valid_1\". That\n  is a usage error, not an RTL problem.\n- Cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): **passed** (selftest +\n  CoreMark, including stalls). Without `NRET=1` the build fails the same\n  way, because main.cpp expects the `_1` ports.\n- cocotb: all suites pass. test_pipeline.py adds 5 directed cases:\n  - a wrong-path SW/JAL/MUL/LW behind taken branches/jumps (no memory,\n    register or redirect side effects);\n  - load-use at a branch target;\n  - load-use under random imem+dmem stalls, with a garbage word on the\n    imem bus during stalls whose rs fields collide with the load rd;\n  - a wrong-path DIV followed by MUL at the jump target;\n  - back-to-back taken branches behind a stalled LOAD, under dmem stalls.\n  `_run` gained optional `iready`/`dready`/`igarbage` knobs. Stores are\n  applied only on dmem-ready cycles.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- ID/EX and EX/MEM data flops no longer reset. Every consumer is gated by\n  a reset valid bit or a reset ctrl bit, and formal (which starts from a\n  symbolic state after reset) passes, but X-propagation in a 4-state\n  simulator could show X on RVFI data fields of non-retiring slots.\n- A spurious load-use (raw word during an imem stall or on a squashed\n  slot) only costs cycles in theory: the slot is already invalid and the\n  PC is already held. CoreMark cycle count should be unchanged.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1625, "cache_read_input_tokens": 127548, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1625}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4ec48193-9760-431e-8182-33e571c58677", "uuid": "34b1a6a6-bb07-462b-9020-500bd64bd482", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:34:10.087Z", "request_id": "req_011CfYDCaVah1NQkCosPpdsq"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01RHVro4SBhEMkegQQgjnZ1d", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4ec48193-9760-431e-8182-33e571c58677", "uuid": "df32159a-d622-483f-8a7a-7b1b9bc4a85f", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:34:10.097Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r2s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes: valid-bit squash pipeline control\n\n## What changed\n\n- **if_stage.sv**: the `(flush||redirect) ? NOP : imem_data` mux is gone.\n  `out.instr = imem_data`, `out.valid = imem_ready` (new `imem_ready`\n  input). The `flush` input is removed. PC priority is unchanged\n  (reset > redirect > !stall > hold).\n- **id_stage.sv**: ports are now `hold`/`squash` (they replace\n  `stall`/`flush`). Decoder, imm_gen, regfile addresses and the ID/EX\n  rd/rs fields all use the raw fetched word. The ID/EX data fields have\n  no reset and no flush and load whenever `!hold`. A separate `valid_q`\n  flop resets to 0 and otherwise loads `in.valid && !squash` when `!hold`.\n- **hazard_unit.sv**: `load_use = id_ex.valid && id_ex.mem_read &&\n  rd!=0 && (rd==imem_data[19:15] || rd==imem_data[24:20])` (raw word).\n  Outputs are `stall_if` (same terms as before),\n  `id_hold = dmem_stall || mdu_stall`,\n  `id_squash = load_use || redirect`, and `stall_ex_mem`/`hold_mem_wb`\n  (unchanged). `flush_if`/`flush_id` are removed.\n- **ex_stage.sv**:\n  - `redirect = in.valid && (taken || jump) && !misalign`.\n  - The EX/MEM register is split. `ctrl_q`/`valid_q` reset to 0 and hold\n    on stall. They capture `ex_valid = in.valid && !mdu_stall`, with\n    reg_write/mem_read/mem_write/is_illegal/is_mdu ANDed with `ex_valid`.\n    The data fields have no reset and hold only on dmem stall. The\n    mdu_stall bubble is therefore now \"valid=0 + side effects cleared\"\n    instead of a full `'0` reset.\n  - Step 6: there is a new dedicated `mem_addr = rs1_fwd + imm` adder,\n    captured into the new `ex_mem_t.mem_addr` field.\n- **mem_stage.sv**: dmem_addr, byte_mask, misalign, load shift and the\n  RVFI aligned_addr now come from `in.mem_addr` instead of\n  `in.alu_result`. `alu_result` still feeds forwarding and writeback.\n- **core_pkg.sv**: adds `mem_addr` to `ex_mem_t`. Comments updated.\n- **core.sv**: rewired. The hazard unit gets `id_ex.valid` and the raw\n  `io_imemData` rs fields. No IO or RVFI changes.\n- **forward_unit.sv**: unchanged. EX/MEM reg_write is valid-qualified\n  at capture.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- **Step 5 not done** (registered forward selects). It is optional in\n  the hypothesis and I left it out to keep the risk and the time budget\n  down.\n- **No extra valid gating on dmem_wen/dmem_ren in mem_stage.** EX/MEM\n  mem_read/mem_write are already cleared for every invalid slot, and\n  ctrl_q resets to 0, so the extra AND would only add logic.\n- The ID/EX and EX/MEM `reg_q.valid` / `reg_q.ctrl` sub-fields are still\n  written (to a constant or unused value) so Verilator sees them driven.\n  `out.valid`/`out.ctrl` are overridden from the separate flops, and\n  synthesis prunes the unused bits.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint (`-Wall`): clean.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  auto nret=1 → wrapper_si + checks_si): **53 passed, 0 failed** on the\n  first attempt. Note: passing `formal/checks.cfg` explicitly forces the\n  nret=2 wrapper and fails at elaboration with \"no io_rvfi_valid_1\". That\n  is a usage error, not an RTL problem.\n- Cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): **passed** (selftest +\n  CoreMark, including stalls). Without