d a stalled load. Two of these failed at first, but the fault was in the stall model I added to the test harness, not in the RTL, and they pass after fixing it.\n\n**Timing:** the old slowest path (redirect → NOP mux → regfile address / flush) is gone. The worst paths are now:\n- regfile → forward mux → ALU → EX/MEM, 20.31 ns\n- regfile → forward mux → branch compare → redirect → PC, 20.29 ns\n\nStep 5, or taking the jump/multiply-divide result mux off the ALU result capture, would be the next thing to try.\n\n**Concern:** the ID/EX and EX/MEM data registers no longer reset. Every consumer is gated by a valid bit or a control bit that does reset, and formal passes. A 4-state simulator could still show X on RVFI data fields of slots that never retire.\n\nThe notes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.", "ttft_ms": 52229, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 418364, "uuid": "120e7d4d-2191-4408-956f-9e69e0266a81", "ttft_stream_ms": 1390, "time_to_request_ms": 44, "first_content_frame_ms": 1390, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}

