{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01MvfC5esFcrwKai7sbvpVq2", "type": "tool_result", "content": "The file /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d9bb7652-2e74-41e3-a4f7-66b9970660e8", "uuid": "5088bb68-3adc-40b3-b671-5fedbd50ac91", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:14:26.119Z", "tool_use_result": {"filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "oldString": "- Formal (`formal/run_all.sh`, checks_si.cfg): see status below.", "newString": "- Formal (`formal/run_all.sh`, checks_si.cfg, ALTOPS): PASS, \"Formal:\n  53 passed, 0 failed\", on the first attempt. This includes pc_fwd,\n  pc_bwd, unique, causal, liveness, ill, reg, cover and every insn_*\n  check.", "originalFile": "# Zero-bubble fetch-stage branch prediction (predecode + 256-entry bimodal BHT)\n\n## What changed\n\n- `rtl/branch_predictor.sv` (new): predecodes the raw `io_imemData` word.\n  BRANCH (1100011) and JAL (1101111) are detected, the B/J immediate is\n  muxed into one `pc + imm` adder, and `pred_taken = !imm[1] && (JAL ||\n  (BRANCH && BHT[pc[9:2]][1]))`. The BHT is 256 x 2-bit saturating\n  counters in flops with synchronous reset to weakly-taken (2'b10). It has\n  a second read port at `upd_idx` for the saturating inc/dec write.\n- `rtl/if_stage.sv`: instantiates the predictor. The PC priority is\n  redirect -> redirect_target, then stall -> hold, then pred_taken ->\n  pred_target, then pc+4. `out.pred_taken = pred_taken && !(flush ||\n  redirect)`, so it is 0 whenever `out.valid` is 0. It also passes the BHT\n  update port through.\n- `rtl/core_pkg.sv`: `pred_taken` bit added to `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t`.\n- `rtl/id_stage.sv`: latches `pred_taken` into ID/EX. Reset and flush\n  clear it through the existing `'0` assignment.\n- `rtl/ex_stage.sv`:\n  `actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault`,\n  `redirect = (actual_taken != pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken)`,\n  `redirect_target = !actual_taken ? pc+4 : is_jump ? jump_target :\n  branch_target`. The BHT update is `en = in.valid && is_branch &&\n  !stall`, `idx = pc[9:2]`, `taken = branch_cond`. `pc_next`, the\n  misalign trap and the RVFI fields are unchanged.\n- `rtl/core.sv`: wires the EX BHT update into `if_stage`. The IO and RVFI\n  ports are unchanged.\n- `test/test_branch_predictor.py` (new): 8 cocotb tests. They cover B/J\n  targets with positive and negative offsets, JAL predicted whatever the\n  BHT holds, BRANCH following the counter MSB, saturation at 3 and at 0,\n  pc[9:2] indexing and aliasing, no prediction when imm[1]=1, and no\n  prediction for non-control opcodes including JALR.\n- `test/test_pipeline.py`: added `branch_predictor.sv` to the source list\n  (the build failed without it).\n\n## Deviations\n\nNone of substance. The BHT uses flops with reset rather than LUT-RAM:\nLUT-RAM cannot be reset to weakly-taken, and flops behave the same in\nVerilator, Yosys formal and Gowin. Predecode does not filter out BRANCH\nfunct3 values 2 and 3 (illegal). If such an instruction is predicted\ntaken, EX sees `is_branch = 0`, so `actual_taken = 0` and it redirects to\npc+4: correct, at the cost of one bubble.\n\n## Correctness argument\n\n- PC is always 4-aligned, so a predicted target is misaligned exactly\n  when imm[1] = 1. Those cases are never predicted, which keeps the\n  prediction consistent with EX's misalign trap (no redirect, pc_next =\n  pc+4).\n- The PC follows a prediction only when it advances with no stall and no\n  redirect. That is exactly the cycle in which ID/EX captures this IF\n  instruction together with its `pred_taken`, so a carried prediction\n  always belongs to the instruction it was made for.\n- A predicted-taken BRANCH or JAL always has the correct target\n  (pc+imm), so EX only has to compare direction.\n\n## Verification (local)\n\n- Verilator lint `-Wall`: clean.\n- cocotb: all tests in `cores/bench/test/` pass. test_pipeline has 11\n  cases and test_branch_predictor has 8.\n- cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`; a plain `make cosim` builds\n  with NRET=2 and fails to compile for this nret=1 core, as the harness\n  would for any nret=1 core): passed on both ELFs.\n- CoreMark with `--bench --istall --dstall`: CRCs correct, \"Correct\n  operation validated\". 4,193,149 bracketed cycles for 10 iterations,\n  about 419k per iteration. The hypothesis puts the baseline at about\n  449k per iteration, so this is about 6.6% fewer cycles, close to its\n  6.7% estimate.\n- Formal (`formal/run_all.sh`, checks_si.cfg): see status below.\n\n## Concerns\n\n- New timing paths: pc reg -> 256:1 BHT read mux -> PC mux; imem data ->\n  imm mux -> 32-bit adder -> PC mux; and EX redirect now also depends on\n  `pred_taken` (one XOR). All of these should be far shorter than the\n  ~200 ns divider path. I did not run `make timing` locally.\n- The flop BHT adds 512 FFs plus two 256:1 x 2-bit read muxes (roughly a\n  few hundred LUTs).\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 68, "oldLines": 7, "newStart": 68, "newLines": 10, "lines": ["   about 419k per iteration. The hypothesis puts the baseline at about", "   449k per iteration, so this is about 6.6% fewer cycles, close to its", "   6.7% estimate.", "-- Formal (`formal/run_all.sh`, checks_si.cfg): see status below.", "+- Formal (`formal/run_all.sh`, checks_si.cfg, ALTOPS): PASS, \"Formal:", "+  53 passed, 0 failed\", on the first attempt. This includes pc_fwd,", "+  pc_bwd, unique, causal, liveness, ill, reg, cover and every insn_*", "+  check.", " ", " ## Concerns", " "]}], "userModified": false, "replaceAll": false}}
