{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfYD6EDX8hw4H7uFrac3m", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CaL7FK5DycvYf7XAhgCmhb", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r2s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# hyp-20260929-003-r2s2: fetch bimodal predictor + registered mispredict redirect\n\n## What changed\n- `rtl/branch_predictor.sv` (new): predecodes the RAW `io_imemData` for BRANCH\n  and JAL, selects the B or J immediate by `instr[3]`, and adds pc+imm. It holds\n  a 256x2b bimodal table indexed by pc[9:2] (async read, weakly-taken `initial`\n  values, no reset), so it can map to LUT-RAM. JAL is always predicted taken.\n  BRANCH is predicted taken when ctr[1] is set. Nothing is predicted when\n  imm[1]=1, and JALR and other opcodes are never predicted. The saturating\n  counter update is computed inside the module from (old ctr, taken).\n- `rtl/if_stage.sv`: instantiates the predictor. PC priority is\n  `kill ? EX/MEM.pc_next : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4`.\n  The NOP mux on out.instr is gone (the word is passed raw), and\n  `out.valid = !flush` and `out.pred_taken = pred_taken && !flush`.\n  Only pc[31:2] is stored, because PC is always aligned.\n- `rtl/core_pkg.sv`: `pred_taken`, `pred_ctr` added to if_id_t/id_ex_t;\n  `mispredict`, `pred_ctr` added to ex_mem_t.\n- `rtl/id_stage.sv`: latches pred_taken/pred_ctr. An invalid fetch\n  (`!in.valid` with no stall) is captured as a full bubble ('0). This is\n  needed because the raw word now reaches the decoder, and its ctrl bits\n  (mem_write, reg_write) must never go downstream.\n- `rtl/ex_stage.sv`: `actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault`\n  and `mispredict = valid && actual_taken != pred_taken`, registered into\n  EX/MEM. New `kill` input: EX/MEM captures a bubble (same arm as mdu_stall),\n  and `mdu_stall` (which is also the MDU start) is gated with `!kill`. The\n  combinational `redirect`/`redirect_target` outputs are removed. pc_next and\n  the misalign trap are unchanged.\n- `rtl/hazard_unit.sv`: `redirect` is replaced by `kill` (= EX/MEM.mispredict,\n  a flop). `flush_if = kill || imem_stall` and\n  `flush_id = (load_use && !dmem_stall) || kill`.\n- `rtl/core.sv`: wires `kill = ex_mem.mispredict` and `redirect_pc = ex_mem.pc_next`.\n  The BHT update comes from EX/MEM: `en = valid && is_branch`,\n  `idx = pc[9:2]`, `taken = branch_taken`, with the carried `pred_ctr`.\n\n## Deviations from the plan\n- **The predicted target uses a 20-bit add, and prediction is suppressed when\n  the target leaves the current 1 MiB region** (carry-out != imm sign).\n  Reason: the redirect is now one cycle late, so the wrong path is 2 deep and\n  W2 is fetched from W1's *prediction*. W1 can be non-code, for example the\n  fall-through after a `ret`. `test/cosim/main.cpp` flags OOB on *every* imem\n  address, so a data word decoded as a JAL with a negative offset near address 0\n  would have failed cosim. With the guard, every predicted fetch stays inside\n  [0, 1 MiB) whenever the PC is. It is exact, because a prediction is only made\n  when the target equals pc+imm. The add is also shorter than 32 bits.\n- The BHT update is driven from the EX/MEM register instead of EX. This keeps\n  the EX branch compare off the LUT-RAM write port. EX/MEM never holds a branch\n  for more than one cycle (it only holds memory ops), so each branch updates\n  exactly once.\n- `mispredict` is not gated with `!kill` inside EX, because the kill arm of\n  EX/MEM already writes '0.\n- `kill` is EX/MEM.mispredict alone (no `valid &&`): every bubble arm zeroes\n  it, and a held EX/MEM always holds a memory op, which cannot mispredict.\n\n## Verification (local)\n- Verilator lint (-Wall): clean.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh`: **53 passed, 0 failed** (first attempt).\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` (with NRET=1 in the environment, because the Makefile\n  cosim-build step defaults to NRET=2): **passed** on selftest and CoreMark,\n  with and without istall/dstall.\n- cocotb: `test_pipeline.py` 17/17 (new cases: predicted-taken loop; a\n  mispredicted BNE whose wrong path W1/W2 are SW/MUL, plus a JALR whose\n  fall-through is a LW, checking no store, retirement or stuck MDU; JAL/JALR\n  call/return; and a mispredict after a dmem-stalled load with imem stalls\n  across the kill cycle, over 4 stall patterns). `test_branch_predictor.py` 3/3.\n  The harness `_run` gained optional istall/dstall callbacks.\n\n## Concerns\n- Gowin may not honour `initial` values on inferred LUT-RAM. This only changes\n  the starting counter state on hardware. IPC is measured in Verilator.\n- The BHT read (pc flop -> LUT-RAM -> ctr[1]) and the 20-bit adder carry both\n  feed the PC-mux select. This path should be much shorter than the old\n  redirect chain, but `make timing` was not run locally because of the time budget.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1157, "cache_read_input_tokens": 121039, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1157}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c07e82fc-6d89-48c2-a049-18dac0607ace", "uuid": "41d3e36f-5ee5-43c6-bb78-8adddd7af477", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:32:44.020Z", "request_id": "req_011CfYD6DjVqjDNyGcTG1Mkt"}
