of\n  EX/MEM already writes '0.\n- `kill` is EX/MEM.mispredict alone (no `valid &&`): every bubble arm zeroes\n  it, and a held EX/MEM always holds a memory op, which cannot mispredict.\n\n## Verification (local)\n- Verilator lint (-Wall): clean.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh`: **53 passed, 0 failed** (first attempt).\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` (with NRET=1 in the environment, because the Makefile\n  cosim-build step defaults to NRET=2): **passed** on selftest and CoreMark,\n  with and without istall/dstall.\n- cocotb: `test_pipeline.py` 17/17 (new cases: predicted-taken loop; a\n  mispredicted BNE whose wrong path W1/W2 are SW/MUL, plus a JALR whose\n  fall-through is a LW, checking no store, retirement or stuck MDU; JAL/JALR\n  call/return; and a mispredict after a dmem-stalled load with imem stalls\n  across the kill cycle, over 4 stall patterns). `test_branch_predictor.py` 3/3.\n  The harness `_run` gained optional istall/dstall callbacks.\n\n## Concerns\n- Gowin may not honour `initial` values on inferred LUT-RAM. This only changes\n  the starting counter state on hardware. IPC is measured in Verilator.\n- The BHT read (pc flop -> LUT-RAM -> ctr[1]) and the 20-bit adder carry both\n  feed the PC-mux select. This path should be much shorter than the old\n  redirect chain, but `make timing` was not run locally because of the time budget.\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}}
