{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYDMxjYgQ34cscizC3Ss","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added one bullet for hyp-20260929-002-r2s1 to the end of `cores/bench/LESSONS.md`. The three earlier lessons are unchanged, and no other file was modified.\n\n**The lesson:** the old design squashed wrong-path work by forcing the fetched instruction to a NOP and resetting the ID/EX flops. That tied the branch redirect to the register-file read, the load-use check and a high-fanout clock-enable net. Clearing only the ID/EX valid bit removed that path, and the speedup matched the prediction with the same cycle count.\n\nIt follows on from the earlier r1s1 lesson, which named the redirect/flush path as the next Fmax limit.\n\nTwo things in the bullet are hedged:\n- **Frequency:** the ~66 MHz figure is my estimate, not a timing report. I scaled the old 48.3 MHz by the +37.69% gain and assumed the cycle count didn't change.\n- **Attribution:** the same change also added a separate address adder for data memory, so the gain can't be credited to the valid-bit squash alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":21989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"output_tokens":356,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a82b8145-33ef-4391-a07a-4bb9a5329cef","uuid":"5b648597-98fd-47c7-8bf3-2947ad9aad57","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:36:00.300Z","request_id":"req_011CfYDMxF2kNoJc6gxTrzbN"}
