{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFBSUNxGEjEX3mwRzZ5frg","type":"tool_result","content":"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r1s0 (regression, +739.85%): Making only DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU a stalling radix-2 sequential unit took Fmax from ~5.4 to ~45 MHz at negligible CoreMark IPC cost, since the combinational `/`/`%` was nearly the whole critical path; it is labelled a regression only because sibling r1s1 also moved MUL into the multi-cycle unit and scored ~1.4% higher, which is inside the ~6% seed spread, so the DSP multiplier is not a significant next Fmax limiter.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r1s1 (improvement, +752.15%): Once DIV/REM and MUL are both in a stalling M-unit, Fmax stops near the ~49 MHz probe ceiling set by the regfile LUTRAM -> EX branch compare -> redirect -> hazard -> ID/EX flush path (~25.6 ns, 17 levels), so moving MUL off EX adds almost nothing; later Fmax work has to shorten redirect/flush, and new stall signals such as mdu_stall must come only from registered ID/EX + done-flop state so they do not lengthen that path.\nCORE_PHILOSOPHY.md\ncore.yaml\nexperiments\ngenerated\nLESSONS.md\nobj_dir\nrtl\ntest\nworktrees","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35614989-ddb1-4d3d-8c57-526fc00421c8","uuid":"a9944053-92d6-4eb4-8e59-bbd6d2fa7363","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:23:10.855Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r1s0 (regression, +739.85%): Making only DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU a stalling radix-2 sequential unit took Fmax from ~5.4 to ~45 MHz at negligible CoreMark IPC cost, since the combinational `/`/`%` was nearly the whole critical path; it is labelled a regression only because sibling r1s1 also moved MUL into the multi-cycle unit and scored ~1.4% higher, which is inside the ~6% seed spread, so the DSP multiplier is not a significant next Fmax limiter.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r1s1 (improvement, +752.15%): Once DIV/REM and MUL are both in a stalling M-unit, Fmax stop