{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYDNozUNm5wJsMjtdisf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MnKokjwAaYQKXiKEb218ZQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/experiments; tail -n 5 log.jsonl | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n    d=json.loads(l)\n    print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k not in ('diff','motivation','hypothesis')})\n\"; tail -c 3000 hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260929-003-r2s2.log","description":"Show recent log entries and agent log tail"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":496,"cache_read_input_tokens":22424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":496},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f121a6-b80e-457a-be4c-5b6a93906dd8","uuid":"3315b9c4-bcbf-43fe-b0ca-aa1b4a97d667","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:36:10.994Z","request_id":"req_011CfYDNoesezit76ATDhWMS"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01MnKokjwAaYQKXiKEb218ZQ", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{'id': 'hyp-20260929-001-r1s0', 'title': 'Replace combinational 32-bit divider with a stalling radix-2 iterative divider', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/divider.sv', 'description': 'New sequential radix-2 restoring divider. Latches operands on start, runs about 33 cycles, fixes up sign, registers the result. Handles RV32M div-by-0 and overflow cases. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS it returns the ALTOPS formula from the latched operands with 1-2 cycle latency.'}, {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"Delete the combinational / and % arms (DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU give 0 or don't-care; the real result comes from divider.sv). Keep MUL* and the ALTOPS MUL* arms unchanged.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': \"Instantiate divider. Start it when ID/EX holds a valid div op that is not active or done. Add a div_busy output. Mux div_result into alu_result on completion. Put a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem-stall hold applies). Record latched operands as rs1_val/rs2_val for a divide's RVFI. Clear done when EX/MEM captures.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add a div_busy input. It asserts stall_if and stall_id (hold, not flush) and does not flush_id. dmem_stall still has priority for EX/MEM hold. Expose a bubble_ex signal (div_busy && !dmem_stall).'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire div_busy and bubble_ex between ex_stage and hazard_unit. Top-level IO unchanged.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Optionally add an is_div bit to ctrl_t, or keep decoding it from alu_op (ALU_DIV..ALU_REMU).'}, {'file': 'rtl/decoder.sv', 'description': 'If ctrl_t.is_div is added, set it for funct7=0000001 with funct3[2]=1. Illegal-default discipline unchanged.'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Remove the combinational DIV/REM checks from the ALU test, since the ALU no longer computes them. Keep all MUL/base-op vectors.'}, {'file': 'test/test_divider.py', 'description': 'New cocotb test for th\n…[15114 of 18186 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:819e03d1edf7e826]…\n+22%, medium confidence.**\\n- **Cycles:** stall cycles from branches and jumps drop from about 357.5k to about 118k. That is about 2 per mispredict or JALR, from roughly 45k mispredicts plus 13.7k JALRs. It works out to about +5% instructions per cycle. Last round the same trace model predicted r1s2's result to within 0.5 points.\\n- **Clock:** the longest path should drop from 17–19 logic levels to about 10–12. It would then be either the execute-stage ALU path or the fetch path through the target adder to the PC, giving roughly 58–63 MHz.\\n\\n**Main risks:** a wrong-path instruction must never write memory or registers or start the multiply/divide unit. And the fetch-stage predecode, adder and PC mux must stay shorter than the execute-stage path, otherwise the clock gain is smaller than estimated.\",\"ttft_ms\":36919,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":184347,\"uuid\":\"39cc927d-6625-447d-91f3-f8dd42f5f411\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":1471,\"time_to_request_ms\":38,\"first_content_frame_ms\":1472,\"queued_turn_count\":0,\"result_index\":0}", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f1f121a6-b80e-457a-be4c-5b6a93906dd8", "uuid": "47f7ae9e-02e5-4640-84b3-494457f3e6ba", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:36:11.080Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "{'id': 'hyp-20260929-001-r1s0', 'title': 'Replace combinational 32-bit divider with a stalling radix-2 iterative divider', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'high'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/divider.sv', 'description': 'New sequential radix-2 restoring divider. Latches operands on start, runs about 33 cycles, fixes up sign, registers the result. Handles RV32M div-by-0 and overflow cases. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS it returns the ALTOPS formula from the latched operands with 1-2 cycle latency.'}, {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': \"Delete the combinational / and % arms (DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU give 0 or don't-care; the real result comes from divider.sv). Keep MUL* and the ALTOPS MUL* arms unchanged.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': \"Instantiate divider. Start it when ID/EX holds a valid div op that is not active or done. Add a div_busy output. Mux div_result into alu_result on completion. Put a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem-stall hold applies). Record latched operands as rs1_val/rs2_val for a divide's RVFI. Clear done when EX/MEM captures.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add a div_busy input. It asserts stall_if and stall_id (hold, not flush) and does not flush_id. dmem_stall still has priority for EX/MEM hold. Expose a bubble_ex signal (div_busy && !dmem_stall).'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire div_busy and bubble_ex between ex_stage and hazard_unit. Top-level IO unchanged.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Optionally add an is_div bit to ctrl_t, or keep decoding it from alu_op (ALU_DIV..ALU_REMU).'}, {'file': 'rtl/decoder.sv', 'description': 'If ctrl_t.is_div is added, set it for funct7=0000001 with funct3[2]=1. Illegal-default discipline unchanged.'}, {'file': 'test/test_alu.py', 'description': 'Remove the combinational DIV/REM checks from the ALU test, since the ALU no longer computes them. Keep all MUL/base-op vectors.'}, {'file': 'test/test_divider.py', 'description': 'New cocotb test for th\n…[15114 of 18186 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:819e03d1edf7e826]…\n+22%, medium confidence.**\\n- **Cycles:** stall cycles from branches and jumps drop from about 357.5k to about 118k. That is about 2 per mispredict or JALR, from roughly 45k mispredicts plus 13.7k JALRs. It works out to about +5% instructions per cycle. Last round the same trace model predicted r1s2's result to within 0.5 points.\\n- **Clock:** the longest path should drop from 17–19 logic levels to about 10–12. It would then be either the execute-stage ALU path or the fetch path through the target adder to the PC, giving roughly 58–63 MHz.\\n\\n**Main risks:** a wrong-path instruction must never write memory or registers or start the multiply/divide unit. And the fetch-stage predecode, adder and PC mux must stay shorter than the execute-stage path, otherwise the clock gain is smaller than estimated.\",\"ttft_ms\":36919,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":184347,\"uuid\":\"39cc927d-6625-447d-91f3-f8dd42f5f411\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":1471,\"time_to_request_ms\":38,\"first_content_frame_ms\":1472,\"queued_turn_count\":0,\"result_index\":0}", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
