{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfYB1ndnd3wyazS4PXsiT", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01D9cygzrhpvGZ8aEeeHNhgp", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r1s0.yaml", "content": "id: hyp-20260929-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Replace combinational 32-bit divider with a stalling radix-2 iterative divider\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Baseline Fmax is 5.44 MHz with a 199.8 ns / 150-logic-level worst path\n  (u_mem.rd -> u_fwd -> u_ex -> u_ex/u_alu -> dmem). That depth, and most of the\n  12.3k LUT4s, comes from the combinational `/` and `%` in alu.sv: Gowin builds\n  DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU as chains of 32 subtract-and-compare stages. Fitness is\n  CoreMark/MHz (~2.23) x Fmax, so the divider sets the clock for every other\n  instruction. CoreMark -O3 runs almost no divides inside the timed window\n  (list, matrix, state and crc kernels use shifts, adds and muls). Making the\n  divider multi-cycle should cost almost no cycles and remove a path that is\n  roughly 5-10x longer than any other path in the core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Remove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU from the combinational ALU and run them on a small\n  sequential divider in EX: restoring, radix-2, one quotient bit per cycle,\n  about 33-34 cycles per divide. Sign is handled outside the loop. The divider\n  holds the pipeline with the existing stall mechanism.\n\n  Divider (new rtl/divider.sv):\n    - On start, latch the raw post-forward operands a_q/b_q (rs1/rs2 as seen\n      in EX on the first cycle), is_signed, and want_rem. Load the magnitudes\n      |a| and |b| (take |x| only for signed ops) into a 32-bit remainder\n      register, a 32-bit dividend/quotient shift register and a 32-bit divisor\n      register. Each cycle does one 33-bit trial subtract and one shift. A\n      6-bit counter drives `done`.\n    - Final fixup: quotient negate = signed && (a[31]^b[31]) && (b != 0);\n      remainder negate = signed && a[31]. Restoring division gives\n      q = all-ones and r = a for b == 0, and the INT_MIN / -1 overflow case\n      becomes q = 0x80000000, r = 0. Both match RV32M with no special-case\n      compare in the loop. Register the fixed-up result, so the output mux\n      only adds one 2:1 level to EX.\n    - Under `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`: the result is the same ALTOPS\n      formula as today ((a_q - b_q) ^ const per op), computed from the\n      latched operands, and latency drops to 1-2 cycles. Formal still\n      covers the start, stall, operand-latch and complete handshake inside\n      the BMC depth, and the liveness check stays short.\n\n  Pipeline integration:\n    - div_busy = ID/EX.valid && is_div_op && !div_done. While it is high:\n      stall_if = 1; stall_id = 1 (hold, no flush; a divide never redirects);\n      EX/MEM takes a bubble (valid=0, reg_write=0, mem_read=mem_write=0,\n      is_illegal=0) so forward_unit and ex_mem_mem_op see nothing.\n      MEM/WB keeps draining normally. dmem_stall keeps priority: if it is\n      active, EX/MEM holds as today and the divider may keep iterating.\n    - Latch the operands only on the start cycle. After that, the older\n      producers leave EX/MEM and MEM/WB, so forwarding would return stale\n      ID/EX.rs?_val.\n    - On done, EX's alu_result mux picks div_result, and EX/MEM captures the\n      divide normally with rs1_val/rs2_val taken from the latched a_q/b_q so\n      RVFI rs?_rdata stay exact. `done` clears on the cycle EX/MEM captures\n      (!stall_ex_mem).\n    - Add an is_div flag to ctrl_t, or decode it from alu_op range 15..18.\n\n  Expected effect: the worst path moves to the forward-mux -> DSP multiplier\n  or forward -> branch compare -> redirect -> PC -> imem path, likely\n  25-45 MHz instead of 5.4. CoreMark/MHz should be within about 1% of today.\n  Net fitness gain should be several hundred percent, far above the 4.6%\n  acceptance bar. LUT4 count should drop sharply (~12.3k -> ~3-4k).\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"New sequential radix-2 restoring divider. Latches operands on start, runs about 33 cycles, fixes up sign, registers the result. Handles RV32M div-by-0 and overflow cases. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS it returns the ALTOPS formula from the latched operands with 1-2 cycle latency.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Delete the combinational / and % arms (DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU give 0 or don't-care; the real result comes from divider.sv). Keep MUL* and the ALTOPS MUL* arms unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate divider. Start it when ID/EX holds a valid div op that is not active or done. Add a div_busy output. Mux div_result into alu_result on completion. Put a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem-stall hold applies). Record latched operands as rs1_val/rs2_val for a divide's RVFI. Clear done when EX/MEM captures.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a div_busy input. It asserts stall_if and stall_id (hold, not flush) and does not flush_id. dmem_stall still has priority for EX/MEM hold. Expose a bubble_ex signal (div_busy && !dmem_stall).\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire div_busy and bubble_ex between ex_stage and hazard_unit. Top-level IO unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Optionally add an is_div bit to ctrl_t, or keep decoding it from alu_op (ALU_DIV..ALU_REMU).\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"If ctrl_t.is_div is added, set it for funct7=0000001 with funct3[2]=1. Illegal-default discipline unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Remove the combinational DIV/REM checks from the ALU test, since the ALU no longer computes them. Keep all MUL/base-op vectors.\"\n  - file: test/test_divider.py\n    description: \"New cocotb test for the clocked divider: port all existing DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU vectors (div-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, sign mixes, random) plus back-to-back ops. Each check pulses start, waits for done and compares the exact bit result.\"\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4362, "cache_read_input_tokens": 48493, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4362}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "fae3cfd0-5907-49f5-93d6-855b373d652c", "uuid": "c30d6c75-5f24-499b-acac-256c95894767", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:06:04.645Z", "request_id": "req_011CfYB1n54Kkq6zu1R1Fct6"}
