 Add a div_busy output. Mux div_result into alu_result on completion. Put a bubble into EX/MEM while busy (unless dmem-stall hold applies). Record latched operands as rs1_val/rs2_val for a divide's RVFI. Clear done when EX/MEM captures.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a div\n…[8030 of 11102 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:840b6f6ef688de2b]…\n : {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_2_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -188.564, \"arrival_ns\": 198.859, \"logic_cells\": 152, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}\nlogic_levels : 148\nformal_passed : true\ncosim_passed : true\nerror : null\nimplementation_notes : \"\"\ntimestamp : \"2026-09-29T18:17:44.361533Z\"\nslot : 2\nround_id : 1\nlesson : \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r1s2 (regression, +6.60%): A fetch-stage predictor (predecoded pc+imm target, 256-entry bimodal BHT, always-taken JAL, EX redirects only on a direction mismatch) gained +6.6% from IPC alone, close to the +7.1% the reference.py trace model predicted, so that model is a reliable IPC estimator; it counts as a regression only because the r1s0/r1s1 siblings that moved the divider off EX scored ~8x higher, and porting it to that ~49 MHz champion must keep the `actual_taken != pred_taken` compare and the pc+4 redirect-target mux from lengthening the now-critical EX branch compare -> redirect -> flush path.\"", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6a70848a-02fd-4e8b-a210-1ad952381f53", "uuid": "83ff41de-aa94-4060-b5bb-cac65571a871", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:23:59.134Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "===== baseline-bench-9db724f improvement 12.12\nid : \"baseline-bench-9db724f\"\ntitle : \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\"\ncategory : \"micro_opt\"\noutcome : \"improvement\"\nfitness : 12.12\ndelta_pct : 0.0\nvs_baseline : 0.0\nfmax_mhz : 5.442\nipc_coremark : 2e-06\ncycles : 4491485\niterations : 10\nlut4 : 12