{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYBBuHfsVygeSLmVPfts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The 256-entry bimodal BHT mispredicts 44.3k times vs 39.8k for 512 entries, with gshare offering little gain, and a 4-entry return stack only recovers ~0.35% of returns—so I'll drop the return stack to keep the redirect path simple and finalize the hypothesis with these numbers.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7232,"cache_read_input_tokens":71424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7232},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"654a98e9-8783-45a8-8f94-b7abe077f5f3","uuid":"8335608e-72c5-4f30-9b7a-e1da31005cc5","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:08:01.040Z","request_id":"req_011CfYBBtrNQQAdH2EX4XrVi","narration_block_indexes":[0]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfYBBuHfsVygeSLmVPfts", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PjtXSocxACNGJx8FqM1kwi", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r1s2.yaml", "content": "id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Zero-bubble fetch-stage branch prediction: predecode + 256-entry bimodal BHT, predicted JAL\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Fmax is pinned at ~5.4 MHz by the combinational divider path\n  (fwd -> EX -> ALU, ~200 ns). Logic outside that path does not affect\n  Fmax, so this hypothesis can only move fitness through IPC, and any\n  IPC gain maps 1:1 onto fitness.\n\n  Every taken control transfer currently costs one fetch slot. Control\n  flow resolves in EX; the instruction fetched behind it (pc+4) is\n  flushed and the target is fetched one cycle later. I measured this on\n  the exact scored binary (-O3, TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000, ITERATIONS=10)\n  with test/cosim/reference.py, between the 0x10000100 and 0x10000104\n  markers:\n    - 2,922,016 retired instructions (~292k per iteration). The champion\n      spends 5.442e6/12.12 = ~449k cycles per iteration (CPI ~1.54).\n    - 529,588 conditional branches (294,425 taken; 235,191 of the taken\n      ones are backward), 49,367 JAL, 13,735 JALR (all returns).\n    - That is 357,527 redirect bubbles, ~35.8k per iteration = ~8.0% of\n      all cycles.\n  Because IF/ID is combinational (the instruction is decoded in the same\n  cycle it is fetched), a predictor placed there can steer the very next\n  fetch and remove the bubble completely for correct predictions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a fetch-stage direction predictor and a predecoded target, and\n  make EX redirect only on mispredictions.\n\n  1. IF predecode (raw io_imemData, not the flushed/NOP'd copy, so\n     redirect isn't on this path): detect BRANCH (opcode 1100011) and JAL\n     (1101111), build the B/J immediate, target = pc + imm (one 32-bit\n     adder; the J/B imm mux feeds it).\n       - JAL: pred_taken = 1.\n       - BRANCH: pred_taken = BHT[pc[9:2]][1].\n       - Never predict taken if imm[1] = 1 (misaligned target). The\n         existing EX misalign-trap path (no redirect, pc_next = pc+4)\n         then stays consistent with the prediction.\n       - JALR: not predicted, and it still redirects exactly as today.\n         A 4-entry return stack would only recover 13.7k bubbles\n         (~0.35%) and would put a 32-bit target compare on the redirect\n         path, so it is deliberately out of scope.\n  2. BHT: 256 x 2-bit saturating counters indexed by pc[9:2]. Reset or\n     initialize them to weakly-taken (2'b10). Flops or LUT-RAM are both\n     fine. The BHT only affects performance, never architectural state,\n     so uninitialized contents are still correct for formal. It is\n     updated from EX when the ID/EX instruction is a valid branch and\n     !stall_ex_mem (a branch held by a dmem stall is counted once), using\n     the resolved branch condition and the ID/EX pc[9:2].\n  3. if_stage next-PC priority: redirect -> redirect_target; else stall\n     -> hold; else pred_taken -> pred_target; else pc+4. io_imemAddr is\n     still the PC register. PC advances through a prediction exactly\n     when the IF instruction is captured into ID/EX (imem stall,\n     load-use and dmem stall all hold the PC), so no wrong-path\n     instruction ever carries a stale prediction.\n  4. Carry pred_taken through if_id_t and id_ex_t. It must be 0 for\n     flushed/invalid IF output, and ID/EX flush zeroes it. In EX:\n       actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault\n                      (today's redirect expression)\n       redirect        = (actual_taken != pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken)\n       redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target)\n                                      : pc + 4\n     A predicted-taken branch or JAL always has the correct target\n     (pc+imm), so no target compare is needed. pc_next / RVFI stay\n     EX-resolved as today, so pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique, liveness and ill\n     checks see the same architectural stream. flush_if/flush_id on\n     redirect are unchanged.\n\n  Trace-driven estimate on the scored binary: with all JALs and BHT-hit\n  branches bubble-free, the remaining bubbles are 44,293 branch\n  mispredicts (256-entry bimodal; 64 entries gives 51,419 and 512 gives\n  39,814) plus 13,735 JALRs = 58,028, down from 357,527. That saves\n  ~30.0k of ~449k cycles per iteration (-6.7% cycles, +7.1% iter/cycle).\n  By comparison, static BTFN+JAL only recovers ~5.2% of cycles, too\n  close to the 4.6% acceptance bar, which is why this uses a dynamic\n  BHT. The added paths are pc reg -> BHT read -> PC mux and imem data ->\n  imm -> adder -> PC mux (roughly 15-20 ns), and the fwd -> branch\n  compare -> BHT write. All of them are far shorter than the 200 ns\n  divider path, so Fmax should stay within P&R noise.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"New module. Combinational predecode of the raw fetched word (BRANCH/JAL detect, B/J immediate, pc+imm target adder, suppress when imm[1]=1). 256x2-bit bimodal BHT read at pc[9:2] (weakly-taken init). Synchronous update port (en, idx=ex_pc[9:2], taken) with saturating increment/decrement. Outputs pred_taken and pred_target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate branch_predictor. next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4. Export pred_taken in the IF/ID bundle, forced to 0 whenever out.valid is 0 (flush/redirect). Pass the BHT update port through from core.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a 'pred_taken' bit to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch in.pred_taken into ID/EX alongside the other fields (reset/flush zeroes it).\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Redirect only on misprediction. actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault. redirect = (actual_taken != in.pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken). redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target) : pc+4. Output the BHT update (en = in.valid && is_branch && !stall, pc, branch_cond). pc_next and the misalign trap logic are unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX BHT update signals into if_stage/branch_predictor. No IO or RVFI changes.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cocotb unit test for branch_predictor: B/J immediate targets for positive and negative offsets; JAL always predicted; BRANCH follows the counter MSB; counters saturate at 0 and 3; no prediction when imm[1]=1; non-control opcodes (incl. JALR) never predict taken.\"\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7232, "cache_read_input_tokens": 71424, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7232}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "654a98e9-8783-45a8-8f94-b7abe077f5f3", "uuid": "53e68256-2c1d-40f1-9135-62013adbad02", "timestamp": "2026-09-29T18:08:23.841Z", "request_id": "req_011CfYBBtrNQQAdH2EX4XrVi"}
