l (the instruction is decoded in the same\n  cycle it is fetched), a predictor placed there can steer the very next\n  fetch and remove the bubble completely for correct predictions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a fetch-stage direction predictor and a predecoded target, and\n  make EX redirect only on mispredictions.\n\n  1. IF predecode (raw io_imemData, not the flushed/NOP'd copy, so\n     redirect isn't on this path): detect BRANCH (opcode 1100011) and JAL\n     (1101111), build the B/J immediate, target = pc + imm (one 32-bit\n     adder; the J/B imm mux feeds it).\n       - JAL: pred_taken = 1.\n       - BRANCH: pred_taken = BHT[pc[9:2]][1].\n       - Never predict taken if imm[1] = 1 (misaligned target). The\n         existing EX misalign-trap path (no redirect, pc_next = pc+4)\n         then stays consistent with the prediction.\n       - JALR: not predicted, and it still redirects exactly as today.\n         A 4-entry return stack would only recover 13.7k bubbles\n         (~0.35%) and would put a 32-bit target compare on the redirect\n         path, so it is deliberately out of scope.\n  2. BHT: 256 x 2-bit saturating counters indexed by pc[9:2]. Reset or\n     initialize them to weakly-taken (2'b10). Flops or LUT-RAM are both\n     fine. The BHT only affects performance, never architectural state,\n     so uninitialized contents are still correct for formal. It is\n     updated from EX when the ID/EX instruction is a valid branch and\n     !stall_ex_mem (a branch held by a dmem stall is counted once), using\n     the resolved branch condition and the ID/EX pc[9:2].\n  3. if_stage next-PC priority: redirect -> redirect_target; else stall\n     -> hold; else pred_taken -> pred_target; else pc+4. io_imemAddr is\n     still the PC register. PC advances through a prediction exactly\n     when the IF instruction is captured into ID/EX (imem stall,\n     load-use and dmem stall all hold the PC), so no wrong-path\n     instruction ever carries a stale prediction.\n  4. Carry pred_taken through if_id_t and id_ex_t. It must be 0 for\n     flushed/invalid IF output, and ID/EX flush zeroes it. In EX:\n       actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault\n                      (today's redirect expression)\n       redirect        = (actual_taken != pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken)\n       redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target)\n                                      : pc + 4\n     A predicted-taken branch or JAL always has the correct target\n     (pc+imm), so no target compare is needed. pc_next / RVFI stay\n     EX-resolved as today, so pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique, liveness and ill\n     checks see the same architectural stream. flush_if/flush_id on\n     redirect are unchanged.\n\n  Trace-driven estimate on the scored binary: with all JALs and BHT-hit\n  branches bubble-free, the remaining bubbles are 44,293 branch\n  mispredicts (256-entry bimodal; 64 entries gives 51,419 and 512 gives\n  39,814) plus 13,735 JALRs = 58,028, down from 357,527. That saves\n  ~30.0k of ~449k cycles per iteration (-6.7% cycles, +7.1% iter/cycle).\n  By comparison, static BTFN+JAL only recovers ~5.2% of cycles, too\n  close to the 4.6% acceptance bar, which is why this uses a dynamic\n  BHT. The added paths are pc reg -> BHT read -> PC mux and imem data ->\n  imm -> adder -> PC mux (roughly 15-20 ns), and the fwd -> branch\n  compare -> BHT write. All of them are far shorter than the 200 ns\n  divider path, so Fmax should stay within P&R noise.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"New module. Combinational predecode of the raw fetched word (BRANCH/JAL detect, B/J immediate, pc+imm target adder, suppress when imm[1]=1). 256x2-bit bimodal BHT read at pc[9:2] (weakly-taken init). Synchronous update port (en, idx=ex_pc[9:2], taken) with saturating increment/decrement. Outputs pred_taken and pred_target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate branch_predictor. next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4. Export pred_taken in the IF/ID bundle, forced to 0 whenever out.valid is 0 (flush/redirect). Pass the BHT update port through from core.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a 'pred_taken' bit to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch in.pred_taken into ID/EX alongside the other fields (reset/flush zeroes it).\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Redirect only on misprediction. actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault. redirect = (actual_taken != in.pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken). redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target) : pc+4. Output the BHT update (en = in.valid && is_branch && !stall, pc, branch_cond). pc_next and the misalign trap logic are unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX BHT update signals into if_stage/branch_predictor. No IO or RVFI changes.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cocotb unit test for branch_predictor: B/J immediate targets for positive and negative offsets; JAL always predicted; BRANCH follows the counter MSB; counters saturate at 0 and 3; no prediction when imm[1]=1; non-control opcodes (incl. JALR) never predict taken.\"\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 1, "oldLines": 77, "newStart": 1, "newLines": 96, "lines": [" id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2", "-title: \"Zero-bubble fetch-stage branch prediction: predecode + 2-bit BHT + return-address stack\"", "+title: \"Zero-bubble fetch-stage branch prediction: predecode + 256-entry bimodal BHT, predicted JAL\"", " category: predictor", " motivation: |", "   Fmax is pinned at ~5.4 MHz by the combinational divider path", "-  (fwd -> EX -> ALU, ~200 ns). Logic outside that path is free for Fmax,", "-  so fitness can only move through IPC. Every taken branch, JAL and JALR", "-  currently costs one fetch slot: control flow resolves in EX, the", "-  instruction fetched behind it (pc+4) is flushed, and the target is", "-  fetched a cycle later. In CoreMark -O3, taken conditional branches plus", "-  JAL/JALR make up roughly 10-14% of retired instructions (list walks,", "-  crc bit loops, matrix inner loops, the state-machine switch, calls and", "-  returns), so about 0.10-0.14 CPI of a ~1.7 CPI total is redirect", "-  bubbles. Because IF/ID is combinational (the instruction is decoded in", "-  the cycle it is fetched), a predictor placed there can steer the very", "-  next fetch and remove the bubble completely for correct predictions.", "+  (fwd -> EX -> ALU, ~200 ns). Logic outside that path does not affect", "+  Fmax, so this hypothesis can only move fitness through IPC, and any", "+  IPC gain maps 1:1 onto fitness.", "+", "+  Every taken control transfer currently costs one fetch slot. Control", "+  flow resolves in EX; the instruction fetched behind it (pc+4) is", "+  flushed and the target is fetched one cycle later. I measured this on", "+  the exact scored binary (-O3, TOTAL_DATA_SIZE=2000, ITERATIONS=10)", "+  with test/cosim/reference.py, between the 0x10000100 and 0x10000104", "+  markers:", "+    - 2,922,016 retired instructions (~292k per iteration). The champion", "+      spends 5.442e6/12.12 = ~449k cycles per iteration (CPI ~1.54).", "+    - 529,588 conditional branches (294,425 taken; 235,191 of the taken", "+      ones are backward), 49,367 JAL, 13,735 JALR (all returns).", "+    - That is 357,527 redirect bubbles, ~35.8k per iteration = ~8.0% of", "+      all cycles.", "+  Because IF/ID is combinational (the instruction is decoded in the same", "+  cycle it is fetched), a predictor placed there can steer the very next", "+  fetch and remove the bubble completely for correct predictions.", " hypothesis: |", "-  Add a fetch-stage predictor that chooses the next PC in the same cycle", "-  the instruction is fetched, and verify it in EX:", "+  Add a fetch-stage direction predictor and a predecoded target, and", "+  make EX redirect only on mispredictions.", " ", "-  1. Predecode in IF (io_imemData -> small decoder -> adder -> PC mux):", "-     - JAL: always predict taken, target = pc + J-imm (skip prediction if", "-       imm[1]=1 so the misaligned-target trap path is unchanged).", "-     - BRANCH: target = pc + B-imm; direction from a 64-entry 2-bit", "-       saturating-counter BHT indexed by pc[7:2]. Counters reset to", "-       \"weakly not-taken\" for forward offsets and \"weakly taken\" for", "-       backward offsets (or all weakly-taken; implementer's choice);", "-       only predict taken if imm[1]=0.", "-     - JALR used as a return (rs1 in {x1,x5}, rd=x0): predict target =", "-       top of a 4-entry return-address stack. JAL/JALR with rd in", "-       {x1,x5} pushes pc+4. RAS/BHT-speculative state is updated only", "-       when the IF instruction is actually accepted into ID/EX", "-       (!imem_stall && !dmem_stall && !load_use && !redirect). Since only", "-       one instruction (the one in EX) can be older-but-unresolved,", "-       nothing on the wrong path ever touches the RAS.", "-  2. next_pc priority in if_stage: redirect > stall(hold) > predicted", "-     target > pc+4. io_imemAddr stays the PC register.", "-  3. ID/EX carries pred_taken (+ pred_target for JALR). EX computes the", "-     architectural next PC exactly as today (including misalign traps ->", "-     pc+4) and raises redirect only when it differs from the prediction:", "-       - branch: pred_taken != (branch_taken && !misalign) -> redirect to", "-         taken ? branch_target : pc+4", "-       - JAL: never redirects when predicted", "-       - JALR: redirect unless pred_taken && pred_target == jalr target", "-     BHT update happens at EX resolve, gated by !stall_ex_mem so a held", "-     branch is only counted once.", "-  4. The redirect-cycle flush (flush_if/flush_id) is unchanged, so a", "-     misprediction costs the same single bubble a taken branch costs", "-     today; correct predictions cost zero. RVFI pc_wdata still comes from", "-     the EX-resolved pc_next, so pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique and liveness", "-     checks see the same architectural stream.", "+  1. IF predecode (raw io_imemData, not the flushed/NOP'd copy, so", "+     redirect isn't on this path): detect BRANCH (opcode 1100011) and JAL", "+     (1101111), build the B/J immediate, target = pc + imm (one 32-bit", "+     adder; the J/B imm mux feeds it).", "+       - JAL: pred_taken = 1.", "+       - BRANCH: pred_taken = BHT[pc[9:2]][1].", "+       - Never predict taken if imm[1] = 1 (misaligned target). The", "+         existing EX misalign-trap path (no redirect, pc_next = pc+4)", "+         then stays consistent with the prediction.", "+       - JALR: not predicted, and it still redirects exactly as today.", "+         A 4-entry return stack would only recover 13.7k bubbles", "+         (~0.35%) and would put a 32-bit target compare on the redirect", "+         path, so it is deliberately out of scope.", "+  2. BHT: 256 x 2-bit saturating counters indexed by pc[9:2]. Reset or", "+     initialize them to weakly-taken (2'b10). Flops or LUT-RAM are both", "+     fine. The BHT only affects performance, never architectural state,", "+     so uninitialized contents are still correct for formal. It is", "+     updated from EX when the ID/EX instruction is a valid branch and", "+     !stall_ex_mem (a branch held by a dmem stall is counted once), using", "+     the resolved branch condition and the ID/EX pc[9:2].", "+  3. if_stage next-PC priority: redirect -> redirect_target; else stall", "+     -> hold; else pred_taken -> pred_target; else pc+4. io_imemAddr is", "+     still the PC register. PC advances through a prediction exactly", "+     when the IF instruction is captured into ID/EX (imem stall,", "+     load-use and dmem stall all hold the PC), so no wrong-path", "+     instruction ever carries a stale prediction.", "+  4. Carry pred_taken through if_id_t and id_ex_t. It must be 0 for", "+     flushed/invalid IF output, and ID/EX flush zeroes it. In EX:", "+       actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault", "+                      (today's redirect expression)", "+       redirect        = (actual_taken != pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken)", "+       redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target)", "+                                      : pc + 4", "+     A predicted-taken branch or JAL always has the correct target", "+     (pc+imm), so no target compare is needed. pc_next / RVFI stay", "+     EX-resolved as today, so pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique, liveness and ill", "+     checks see the same architectural stream. flush_if/flush_id on", "+     redirect are unchanged.", " ", "-  Expected: ~85-90% of taken control transfers become zero-bubble", "-  (all JALs, most loop back-edges and returns), minus a small number of", "-  new mispredicts on not-taken branches predicted taken. Net ~0.08-0.10", "-  CPI saved (~5-7% IPC). The added logic (predecode adder, 128-bit BHT,", "-  4x32 RAS, 32-bit JALR compare) sits entirely off the 200 ns divider", "-  path, so Fmax should be unchanged within P&R noise and the IPC gain", "-  maps 1:1 onto fitness.", "+  Trace-driven estimate on the scored binary: with all JALs and BHT-hit", "+  branches bubble-free, the remaining bubbles are 44,293 branch", "+  mispredicts (256-entry bimodal; 64 entries gives 51,419 and 512 gives", "+  39,814) plus 13,735 JALRs = 58,028, down from 357,527. That saves", "+  ~30.0k of ~449k cycles per iteration (-6.7% cycles, +7.1% iter/cycle).", "+  By comparison, static BTFN+JAL only recovers ~5.2% of cycles, too", "+  close to the 4.6% acceptance bar, which is why this uses a dynamic", "+  BHT. The added paths are pc reg -> BHT read -> PC mux and imem data ->", "+  imm -> adder -> PC mux (roughly 15-20 ns), and the fwd -> branch", "+  compare -> BHT write. All of them are far shorter than the 200 ns", "+  divider path, so Fmax should stay within P&R noise.", " expected_impact:", "-  fitness_delta_pct: 6", "+  fitness_delta_pct: 7", "   confidence: medium", " changes:", "   - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv", "-    description: \"New module: IF-stage predecode of io_imemData (JAL/BRANCH/JALR-return detection, B/J immediate, pc+imm target adder), 64x2-bit BHT indexed by pc[7:2] with EX-side update port, 4-entry RAS with push/pop gated on IF-accept. Outputs pred_taken and pred_target.\"", "+    description: \"New module. Combinational predecode of the raw fetched word (BRANCH/JAL detect, B/J immediate, pc+imm target adder, suppress when imm[1]=1). 256x2-bit bimodal BHT read at pc[9:2] (weakly-taken init). Synchronous update port (en, idx=ex_pc[9:2], taken) with saturating increment/decrement. Outputs pred_taken and pred_target.\"", "   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv", "-    description: \"Instantiate/consume the predictor; next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4. Export pred_taken/pred_target in the IF/ID bundle.\"", "+    description: \"Instantiate branch_predictor. next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4. Export pred_taken in the IF/ID bundle, forced to 0 whenever out.valid is 0 (flush/redirect). Pass the BHT update port through from core.\"", "   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv", "-    description: \"Add pred_taken (1b) and pred_target (32b) to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"", "+    description: \"Add a 'pred_taken' bit to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"", "   - file: rtl/id_stage.sv", "-    description: \"Latch pred_taken/pred_target into ID/EX (cleared on flush so bubbles never predict).\"", "+    description: \"Latch in.pred_taken into ID/EX alongside the other fields (reset/flush zeroes it).\"", "   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv", "-    description: \"Replace 'redirect on any taken branch/jump' with 'redirect on misprediction': compute the architectural next PC as today (misalign -> pc+4) and redirect only when it disagrees with the IF prediction; redirect_target becomes the architectural next PC (pc+4 for predicted-taken-but-not-taken). Emit BHT update (pc, taken, is_branch, valid, !stall).\"", "+    description: \"Redirect only on misprediction. actual_taken = (branch_taken || is_jump) && !misalign_fault. redirect = (actual_taken != in.pred_taken) || (is_jalr && actual_taken). redirect_target = actual_taken ? (is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target) : pc+4. Output the BHT update (en = in.valid && is_branch && !stall, pc, branch_cond). pc_next and the misalign trap logic are unchanged.\"", "   - file: rtl/core.sv", "-    description: \"Wire predictor update port from EX, IF-accept strobe (from hazard signals) to the RAS/BHT, and the new bundle fields.\"", "+    description: \"Wire the EX BHT update signals into if_stage/branch_predictor. No IO or RVFI changes.\"", "   - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py", "-    description: \"cocotb unit test: BHT saturation/prediction, RAS push/pop/overflow wrap, predecode targets for JAL/B-type with positive/negative offsets, and no prediction for imm[1]=1 targets.\"", "+    description: \"Cocotb unit test for branch_predictor: B/J immediate targets for positive and negative offsets; JAL always predicted; BRANCH follows the counter MSB; counters saturate at 0 and 3; no prediction when imm[1]=1; non-control opcodes (incl. JALR) never predict taken.\""]}], "originalFile": "id: hyp-20260929-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Zero-bubble fetch-stage branch prediction: predecode + 2-bit BHT + return-address stack\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Fmax is pinned at ~5.4 MHz by the combinational divider path\n  (fwd -> EX -> ALU, ~200 ns). Logic outside that path is free for Fmax,\n  so fitness can only move through IPC. Every taken branch, JAL and JALR\n  currently costs one fetch slot: control flow resolves in EX, the\n  instruction fetched behind it (pc+4) is flushed, and the target is\n  fetched a cycle later. In CoreMark -O3, taken conditional branches plus\n  JAL/JALR make up roughly 10-14% of retired instructions (list walks,\n  crc bit loops, matrix inner loops, the state-machine switch, calls and\n  returns), so about 0.10-0.14 CPI of a ~1.7 CPI total is redirect\n  bubbles. Because IF/ID is combinational (the instruction is decoded in\n  the cycle it is fetched), a predictor placed there can steer the very\n  next fetch and remove the bubble completely for correct predictions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a fetch-stage predictor that chooses the next PC in the same cycle\n  the instruction is fetched, and verify it in EX:\n\n  1. Predecode in IF (io_imemData -> small decoder -> adder -> PC mux):\n     - JAL: always predict taken, target = pc + J-imm (skip prediction if\n       imm[1]=1 so the misaligned-target trap path is unchanged).\n     - BRANCH: target = pc + B-imm; direction from a 64-entry 2-bit\n       saturating-counter BHT indexed by pc[7:2]. Counters reset to\n       \"weakly not-taken\" for forward offsets and \"weakly taken\" for\n       backward offsets (or all weakly-taken; implementer's choice);\n       only predict taken if imm[1]=0.\n     - JALR used as a return (rs1 in {x1,x5}, rd=x0): predict target =\n       top of a 4-entry return-address stack. JAL/JALR with rd in\n       {x1,x5} pushes pc+4. RAS/BHT-speculative state is updated only\n       when the IF instruction is actually accepted into ID/EX\n       (!imem_stall && !dmem_stall && !load_use && !redirect). Since only\n       one instruction (the one in EX) can be older-but-unresolved,\n       nothing on the wrong path ever touches the RAS.\n  2. next_pc priority in if_stage: redirect > stall(hold) > predicted\n     target > pc+4. io_imemAddr stays the PC register.\n  3. ID/EX carries pred_taken (+ pred_target for JALR). EX computes the\n     architectural next PC exactly as today (including misalign traps ->\n     pc+4) and raises redirect only when it differs from the prediction:\n       - branch: pred_taken != (branch_taken && !misalign) -> redirect to\n         taken ? branch_target : pc+4\n       - JAL: never redirects when predicted\n       - JALR: redirect unless pred_taken && pred_target == jalr target\n     BHT update happens at EX resolve, gated by !stall_ex_mem so a held\n     branch is only counted once.\n  4. The redirect-cycle flush (flush_if/flush_id) is unchanged, so a\n     misprediction costs the same single bubble a taken branch costs\n     today; correct predictions cost zero. RVFI pc_wdata still comes from\n     the EX-resolved pc_next, so pc_fwd/pc_bwd, unique and liveness\n     checks see the same architectural stream.\n\n  Expected: ~85-90% of taken control transfers become zero-bubble\n  (all JALs, most loop back-edges and returns), minus a small number of\n  new mispredicts on not-taken branches predicted taken. Net ~0.08-0.10\n  CPI saved (~5-7% IPC). The added logic (predecode adder, 128-bit BHT,\n  4x32 RAS, 32-bit JALR compare) sits entirely off the 200 ns divider\n  path, so Fmax should be unchanged within P&R noise and the IPC gain\n  maps 1:1 onto fitness.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"New module: IF-stage predecode of io_imemData (JAL/BRANCH/JALR-return detection, B/J immediate, pc+imm target adder), 64x2-bit BHT indexed by pc[7:2] with EX-side update port, 4-entry RAS with push/pop gated on IF-accept. Outputs pred_taken and pred_target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate/consume the predictor; next_pc = redirect ? redirect_target : stall ? pc : pred_taken ? pred_target : pc+4. Export pred_taken/pred_target in the IF/ID bundle.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add pred_taken (1b) and pred_target (32b) to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch pred_taken/pred_target into ID/EX (cleared on flush so bubbles never predict).\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace 'redirect on any taken branch/jump' with 'redirect on misprediction': compute the architectural next PC as today (misalign -> pc+4) and redirect only when it disagrees with the IF prediction; redirect_target becomes the architectural next PC (pc+4 for predicted-taken-but-not-taken). Emit BHT update (pc, taken, is_branch, valid, !stall).\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor update port from EX, IF-accept strobe (from hazard signals) to the RAS/BHT, and the new bundle fields.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"cocotb unit test: BHT saturation/prediction, RAS push/pop/overflow wrap, predecode targets for JAL/B-type with positive/negative offsets, and no prediction for imm[1]=1 targets.\"\n", "userModified": false}}
