{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYDbkzkJNGPTfYrazdRL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KyNX2QJLKXeok6voe6G2XE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-opus-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-003-r3s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r3s2.yaml","content":"id: hyp-20260929-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"PC-indexed LUTRAM BTB (no imem predecode) with registered-select EX verify/replay\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  On the r2s1 champion (66.6 MHz, worst path ID/EX -> fwd mux -> ALU -> EX/MEM,\n  20.3 ns) every taken branch and every JAL/JALR costs one bubble (EX redirect\n  squashes the one wrong-path fetch). Both earlier predictor attempts (r1s2,\n  r2s2) got the ~5-7% IPC but lost Fmax because the prediction was built from\n  the fetched word: imem_data -> predecode -> imm -> pc+imm adder -> PC mux.\n  A BTB indexed by the PC *register* removes imem_data from the fetch-predict\n  path entirely, so the prediction path is flop -> LUTRAM -> tag compare ->\n  PC mux and stays well under the ~15 ns EX -> ALU path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 64-entry direct-mapped BTB (LUTRAM, async read, index pc[7:2], partial\n  tag, 18-bit word target, 2-bit counter) read with the PC register. If hit &&\n  ctr[1], the sequential next PC becomes the stored target (zero-bubble taken\n  branch / JAL). The seq_next = hit ? tgt : pc+4 mux is computed in parallel\n  and feeds the existing redirect > stall > advance PC mux, so the load-use and\n  redirect paths are unchanged. pred_taken and the predicted target ride in\n  ID/EX. EX keeps all new mux selects on registered or early (flop-only) bits:\n  target_ok = (is_branch || JAL) && pred_target == pc+imm (flop-only adder);\n  replay = pred_taken && !target_ok (kill own slot, redirect to own pc,\n  invalidate entry) ; otherwise predicted-taken branches redirect to pc+4 only\n  when !branch_cond, and unpredicted ones redirect exactly as today. BTB\n  updates are registered and written one cycle after EX. Expect ~5-7% fewer\n  cycles at unchanged Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/btb.sv\n    description: \"New module: 64-entry direct-mapped BTB in LUTRAM (async read, sync write).\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Read BTB with pc; seq_next = hit&&ctr[1] ? target : pc+4; output pred bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add pred_taken / pred_target fields to if_id_t and id_ex_t.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch pred_taken / pred_target into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Verify prediction, replay on bad target, registered-select redirect target, BTB update.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire BTB and update port.\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13064,"cache_read_input_tokens":53778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13064},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b141ed81-537f-4d6c-99e8-fe2d72835635","uuid":"bbde04d8-10f2-4da8-8177-3936de480ec9","timestamp":"2026-09-29T18:39:15.537Z","request_id":"req_011CfYDbkYTfAHLKbHwEwU6t"}
